# Copy to .env locally. Do not commit .env.
# Fill only the targets this project uses.
# Specs must not read process.env. Config and fixtures resolve URLs.
# Never derive an API host from a UI host.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simple project (starter default)
# One UI app + one API. Playwright config reads these names.
# Register extra names in .cursor/rules/00-project-map.mdc before using them.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
UI_BASE_URL=
API_BASE_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Multi-target project (examples only — not registered yet)
# Use this when the product has more than one UI app or API service.
#
# 1. Uncomment only names this application actually has.
# 2. Register the same names in .cursor/rules/00-project-map.mdc.
# 3. Point Page Objects, API clients, and setup at those registered targets.
# 4. Extend .github/workflows/playwright.yml env mapping only after registration.
#
# Do not copy every example "just in case".
# Do not invent names in specs, plans, or clients first.
# Setup/cleanup uses one of the registered names below — there is no global
# precondition API URL. UI_PRECONDITION_API_BASE_URL is legacy only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# UI applications / microfrontends
# CUSTOMER_APP_URL=
# ADMIN_APP_URL=
# CHECKOUT_APP_URL=

# API / microservices
# AUTH_API_URL=
# USERS_API_URL=
# ORDERS_API_URL=
# PAYMENTS_API_URL=

# External or partner systems
# EXTERNAL_PARTNER_API_URL=
